cabal-version:      2.4
name:               req
version:            3.13.4
synopsis:           WASI stub: HTTP is unavailable in a browser
description:
    A drop-in replacement for the @req@ package used when building hledger for
    wasm32-wasi.
    .
    The only use of @req@ in hledger is the @setup@ command's \"is this the
    latest version?\" check, which fetches a page from hledger.org. A browser
    cannot reach arbitrary hosts anyway, and hledger already wraps every one of
    those calls in @try@\/@catch@ and degrades to \"unknown\", so this stub simply
    throws.
    .
    Stubbing @req@ and @http-client@ together is what removes the whole C
    dependency tree that made a wasm build impossible:
    @req -> http-client-tls -> tls -> crypton -> memory -> basement@. The
    @basement@ header has no wasm32 branch, and patching it only reveals the
    next blockers (@crypton@'s x86 intrinsics, @network@'s raw sockets, @zlib@'s
    @pkg-config@), so removing the subtree is the only tractable route.
    .
    The version number matches the real @req@ so hledger's version bounds are
    satisfied unchanged.
    .
    The module interface mirrors the BSD-3-Clause @req@ package by Mark Karpov
    and contributors.
license:            BSD-3-Clause
build-type:         Simple
category:           Network

library
    exposed-modules:  Network.HTTP.Req
    build-depends:    base >=4 && <5, bytestring, text, http-client
    hs-source-dirs:   .
    default-language: Haskell2010
